cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Python static analysers – test environment"
abstract: >-
  Docker-based test environment for comparing eleven static analysers for
  Python (PythonTA, Pylint, Flake8, Pyflakes, Pycodestyle, Prospector, Ruff,
  Mypy, Pyright, Bandit and Semgrep CE) on three test datasets (CODEVIOLATION,
  QuixBugs and YesWeHack Vulnerable Code Snippets) with default settings.
  Used in the bachelor's thesis "Python – Staattinen analyysi"
  (LUT University, 2026).
authors:
  - family-names: Helin
    given-names: Tomi
    affiliation: LUT University
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-11
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Swinkkel/python-static-analyzers-test-environment"
